{"step_index":912,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T14:11:54Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-10T18:11:54+04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-10T18:11:54+04:00\nFile Path: `file:///home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/centreon-map-chain-report.md`\nTotal Lines: 74\nTotal Bytes: 5024\nShowing lines 1 to 74\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Centreon Map Integration & Reverse Proxy Chain Report\n2: \n3: ## 1. Executive Summary\n4: \n5: The entire communication chain for **Centreon Map** (`172.30.198.50:9443`) through the Reverse Proxy **`th2-revproxyp-fe1`** (`172.30.198.33:9443`) and the Central Backend **`th2-centprop-be1`** (`172.30.198.49`) has been fully established, secured with a dedicated Let's Encrypt production certificate, and verified.\n6: \n7: ---\n8: \n9: ## 2. Key Actions Performed & Milestones\n10: \n11: ### A. Passwordless DNS-01 Challenge via `th2-dnsp-mst1`\n12: 1. **Direct Master Authentication**:\n13:    * Verified passwordless SSH access to the authoritative PowerDNS master **`th2-dnsp-mst1`** (`superuser@172.30.198.162:30`) using your ED25519 SSH key (`~/.ssh/id_ed25519`).\n14:    * Confirmed passwordless sudo rights for `pdnsutil`. No HTTP REST API or external API keys were needed.\n15: 2. **Dynamic Record Management**:\n16:    * Updated the Certbot DNS-01 authentication hook ([`pdns-auth-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-auth-hook.sh)) and cleanup hook ([`pdns-cleanup-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-cleanup-hook.sh)).\n17:    * Challenges are directly injected into zone `outremer-telecom.fr` via `pdnsutil replace-rrset` and `pdnsutil increase-serial`.\n18:    * Propagation was verified against public resolvers (Google DoH and Cloudflare DoH) before returning to Certbot.\n19: 3. **Production Certificate Issued**:\n20:    * **Domain**: `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`\n21:    * **Issuer**: `Let's Encrypt (CN = YE2)`\n22:    * **Validity**: September 10, 2026 to December 9, 2026\n23:    * **SAN**: `DNS:map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`\n24: \n25: ---\n26: \n27: ### B. Dedicated Certificate & Nginx Vhost on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`\n28: \n29: As requested, rather than coupling the configuration into the existing file, a **dedicated, independent architecture** was deployed on the reverse proxy:\n30: \n31: 1. **Certificate Deployment**:\n32:    * Saved into [`/etc/letsencrypt/live/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/`](file:///etc/letsencrypt/live/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/) (`fullchain.pem`, `privkey.pem`, `cert.pem`, `chain.pem`) with strict permissions (`0644` / `0600`).\n33: 2. **Dedicated Vhost Created**:\n34:    * File: [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf)\n35:    * Enabled via symlink in [`/etc/nginx/sites-enabled/`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-enabled/).\n36:    * Listens explicitly on `172.30.198.33:9443` (internal DMZ) and `109.62.64.18:9443` (public VIP).\n37:    * Points to upstream `https://172.30.198.50:9443` with `proxy_ssl_verify off;`.\n38:    * Dedicated access and error logs:\n39:      * `/var/log/nginx/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr-access.log`\n40:      * `/var/log/nginx/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr-error.log`\n41:    * Automatic redirect `/` $\\rightarrow$ `/centreon-map/`.\n42:    * Preserved headers: `Host $http_host;`, `X-Forwarded-Proto https;`, `X-Forwarded-Port 9443;`.\n43:    * Cleaned up [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf) to remove all port `9443` blocks.\n44: 3. **Nginx Reload**:\n45:    * `nginx -t`: **Syntax OK, test successful**.\n46:    * Reloaded without downtime.\n47: \n48: ---\n49: \n50: ## 3. End-to-End Verification Results\n51: \n52: ```mermaid\n53: flowchart LR\n54:     Central[\"th2-centprop-be1\\n(172.30.198.49)\\nCentreon Central PHP\"] -->|\"HTTPS :9443\\n(Strict TLS Verified)\"| RevProxy[\"th2-revproxyp-fe1\\n(172.30.198.33)\\nNginx Proxy\"]\n55:     ExtUser[\"External Browser\\n(map.extranetclient...)\"] -->|\"HTTPS :9443\\n(Valid Public Cert)\"| RevProxy\n56:     RevProxy -->|\"HTTPS :9443 (TLS)\\nproxy_ssl_verify off\"| Map[\"th2-centprop-map\\n(172.30.198.50)\\nTomcat Engine\"]\n57: ```\n58: \n59: | Source / Target | Test Command | Result | Status |\n60: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: |\n61: | **Local Machine $\\rightarrow$ Port 9443** | `openssl s_client -connect 172.30.198.33:9443` | `CN=map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`, Issuer `Let's Encrypt (YE2)` | **VERIFIED** |\n62: | **Local Machine $\\rightarrow$ Port 9443** | `curl -sS -I https://map.extranetclient...:9443/` | `HTTP/2 301` $\\rightarrow$ `location: .../centreon-map/` (Strict TLS OK, no `-k`) | **VERIFIED** |\n63: | **Central Backend (`.49`) $\\rightarrow$ Reverse Proxy** | `curl -sS -I https://map.extranetclient...:9443/` | `HTTP/2 301` (Strict TLS OK, no `-k`, `/etc/hosts` routing OK) | **VERIFIED** |\n64: | **Central Backend (`.49`) $\\rightarrow$ Centreon Map** | `curl -sS -I https://map.extranetclient...:9443/centreon-map/` | `HTTP/2 400/401` (Centreon Map application response reached) | **VERIFIED** |\n65: \n66: ---\n67: \n68: ## 4. Final Verification in the Centreon Web UI\n69: \n70: You can now return to the Centreon Web Interface:\n71: 1. Navigate to: **`Administration > Extensions > Options`**.\n72: 2. Under the Map server settings, click **\"Test connection to server\"**.\n73: 3. Because the certificate is now natively trusted by PHP cURL with an exact SAN match for `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`, the test will succeed with a green status.\n74: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
