{"step_index":938,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T14:13:07Z","thinking":"**Isolating the problematic header**\n\nThe 400 error from Tomcat, with an HTML body, confirms the issue lies in the headers sent from Nginx. Examining `proxy.conf` and `03-map...conf` is the next step. To pinpoint the offending header, each header will be individually tested by directly curling the Tomcat instance. The headers to test are `Upgrade`, `Connection`, `Host`, `X-Real-IP`, and `Forwarded`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/home/koby/.ansible/kssh th2-revproxyp-fe1 'python3 -c \"\nimport urllib.request, ssl\nctx = ssl._create_unverified_context()\n\nheaders_list = [\n    (\\\"Forwarded\\\", \\\"for=172.30.198.33;proto=https\\\"),\n    (\\\"X-Forwarded-Host\\\", \\\"map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\\\"),\n    (\\\"X-Forwarded-Port\\\", \\\"9443\\\"),\n    (\\\"X-Forwarded-Proto\\\", \\\"https\\\"),\n    (\\\"X-Forwarded-Ssl\\\", \\\"on\\\"),\n    (\\\"X-Forwarded-For\\\", \\\"172.30.198.33\\\"),\n    (\\\"X-Real-IP\\\", \\\"172.30.198.33\\\"),\n    (\\\"Host\\\", \\\"map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443\\\"),\n    (\\\"Host\\\", \\\"map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\\\"),\n]\n\nfor name, val in headers_list:\n    req = urllib.request.Request(\\\"https://172.30.198.50:9443/centreon-map/api/latest/actuator/health\\\", headers={name: val})\n    try:\n        resp = urllib.request.urlopen(req, context=ctx)\n        print(f\\\"{name}: {val} -> {resp.status}\\\")\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n        print(f\\\"{name}: {val} -> {e.code}\\\")\n\"'","Cwd":"/home/koby","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Testing headers against Tomcat","toolSummary":"Test individual headers against Tomcat"}}]}
